---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Us"
  description="Learn about GST Calculator India — a free, fast, and accurate tool for calculating GST, CGST, SGST, and IGST."
  path="/about"
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6 sm:py-20">
    <header class="text-center">
      <p class="classy-label">Our Story</p>
      <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl sm:text-5xl">About Us</h1>
      <div class="classy-divider mt-6"></div>
      <p class="mt-6 text-muted dark:text-cream/60">
        Making GST calculations clear, considered, and accessible for all.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose-classy mt-12">
      <section>
        <h2>Our Purpose</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          GST Calculator India was established to serve businesses, professionals, and consumers who require swift, dependable tax computations. Whether adding GST to a base figure or extracting it from an inclusive amount, our instrument delivers immediate, accurate results.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What We Provide</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3">
          <li>Add GST to any base price at standard or custom rates</li>
          <li>Remove GST from GST-inclusive prices</li>
          <li>Automatic CGST and SGST apportionment for intra-state transactions</li>
          <li>IGST computation for inter-state transactions</li>
          <li>Support for all common GST slabs: 0%, 5%, 12%, 18%, and 28%</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Our Approach</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Built with care and precision, this calculator operates entirely within your browser — your figures never leave your device. The interface is designed for clarity, with full support for both light and dark presentation.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>A Note of Caution</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          This instrument is intended for quick estimates and general reference. For official filings, invoicing, and compliance, we recommend consulting a qualified chartered accountant or tax professional. Please refer to our <a href="/disclaimer">Disclaimer</a> for further particulars.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
